= The Three Death Sentences

On March 10, Parliament begins debating the execution of Deniz Gezmiş, Yusuf Aslan, and Hüseyin İnan, three revolutionary students sentenced to death by the Ankara Martial Law Court. İnönü, Ecevit, and many of our fellow CHP deputies strongly oppose the executions, arguing that taking the lives of these young men will do little to resolve the political violence that has troubled Turkey. However, the debate quickly turns into another confrontation between the CHP and AP when an AP spokesman, Seyfi Öztürk, accuses the Left of Center movement of helping create the political unrest that led to the March 12 Memorandum.

CHP deputy Necdet Uğur responds furiously, condemning the attempt to hide behind military prosecutors in order to intimidate and discredit our party. Despite our objections, the parliamentary majority remains firmly in favor of the executions, with AP, MGP, and several CHP deputies supporting them. When the votes are finally counted, the death sentences are approved by 238 votes to 53, with six abstentions. Yet İnönü has no intention of allowing the matter to end here.

